<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>4.1.6: Practice</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m00853</md:content-id>
    <md:title>4.1.6: Practice</md:title>
    <md:uuid>4a5b67a7-0f5a-49fa-9bc3-f3b67b2e08cd</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><para dir="ltr">Complete the following questions to practice the skills you have learned in this lesson.</para>

<para>For questions 1 - 4, use the following scenario.
</para>
<blockquote>The relationship between the amount of time a car is parked, in hours, and the cost of parking, in dollars, can be described with a function.</blockquote>
<section class="check-understanding"><exercise data-content-id="e3163c09-c634-4311-89e2-ed8c7dcc3542"><problem><para>
      <para>Identify the independent variable in this function.</para>
      </para></problem><solution><para>Amount of time car is parked</para><para>
      <para>The correct answer is the independent variable is the amount of time the car is parked. </para>
    </para></solution></exercise></section><!-- New pset with 3 attemps -->
<section class="check-understanding"><exercise data-content-id="90dae51d-bab9-48b6-8f3f-2591b15904e4"><problem><para>
      <para>Suppose it costs $3 per hour to park, with a maximum cost of $12. Here is a graph of the situation.</para>
        <figure><media alt=""><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/25e5503db717b9e7113c3af27bc4b60c4bb4b73a"/></media></figure><para>What does the point \((2,6)\) mean in this situation?</para>
      </para><para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>2 hours of parking costs $6 per hour</para><para>6 hours of parking costs $2 per hour</para><para>2 hours of parking costs a total of $6</para><para>6 hours of parking costs a total of $2</para></problem><solution><para>2 hours of parking costs a total of $6</para><para>
      <para>The correct answer is 2 hours of parking costs a total of $6. </para>
    </para></solution></exercise></section></section>
</content>
